# TypeScript security

The always-on security rule wins if this file disagrees with it.

## Secrets

```typescript
// Never commit a literal secret.
const apiKey = process.env.SOME_SERVER_SECRET;
if (!apiKey) {
  throw new Error("SOME_SERVER_SECRET is not configured");
}
```

- `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` is copied into the browser bundle. Treat it as public. Never put a key, password, token, PEM, or KEK behind that prefix.
- Do not read a server-only secret from a client component.
- Missing required config fails closed. Do not substitute an empty string or a committed default outside the documented local compose path.
